{"x":10,"y":2,"captures":[[{"rule":0,"flash":[],"flips":[]}]],"p1s":5,"p2s":5,"eb":0,"z":"red/75794f5d555e4848424f5f4a3178227e37342a74642f333f242569356d","u":1,"c":"42","dialog":[[{"buttons":[{"name":"Skip Tutorial","link":""},{"name":"Start Tutorial","direction":1}],"content":"<p>Welcome to the Basics Tutorial.</p><p>I'll cover the layout and gameplay for Triple Triad and introduce you to the concepts of card ranks and captures.</p>"},{"buttons":[{"name":"Back","direction":-1},{"name":"Next","direction":1}],"content":"<p>Each player starts with five of their own cards.</p><p>Your cards are blue, positioned along the left and your opponents are red, positioned along the right.</p><p>The numbers on each card, called ranks, correspond to each side of the card.</p>"},{"buttons":[{"name":"Back","direction":-1},{"name":"Next","direction":1}],"content":"<p>Behind me is the play area. It consists of nine available positions to place cards arranged in a 3 x 3 grid.</p><p>Each player's score is shown below their cards and the little coin under me is a turn marker.</p>"},{"buttons":[{"name":"Back","direction":-1},{"name":"Next","direction":1}],"content":"<p>A random player is chosen to start.</p><p>Each player takes turns placing a card from their hand onto the play area.</p><p>The objective is to out-rank your opponent's adjacent cards and capture them."},{"buttons":[{"name":"Back","direction":-1},{"name":"Okay!","direction":1}],"content":"<p>The game behind us has been set up for a quick demonstration. Let's watch!</p>"}],[]],"gameover":[]}
